      "source": [
        "# Conclusions\n",
        "\n",
        "- Both Google Reviews and Trustpilot revealed identical patterns in negative feedback themes and emotion distribution, demonstrating robust methodology and confirming that operational issues are systemic rather than platform-specific.\n",
        "  \n",
        "- BERT-based emotion analysis effectively identified anger and sadness as dominant emotions in negative reviews, though occasional misclassification (detecting joy in negative content) indicates need for additional fine-tuning to optimize accuracy.\n",
        "\n",
        "- BERTopic successfully clustered negative reviews around key operational issues, providing transparent and interpretable thematic groupings with lower computational requirements, making it ideal for rapid analysis and operational monitoring.\n",
        "  \n",
        "- LLMs excel at synthesizing complex topics into actionable business recommendations with strategic clarity, however they sacrifice transparency and require higher computational resources compared to traditional models like LDA, which are simpler and faster but need manual interpretation.\n",
        "  \n",
        "- Overall, combining LLM-driven insight extraction with traditional topic modeling and BERT-based sentiment analysis delivers both analytical depth and actionable clarity, enabling efficient translation of customer feedback into operational improvements.\n",
        "\n",
